<title>SINGAPORE: Lim Kah Ngam sees slower growth in 1997.</title>
<headline>Lim Kah Ngam sees slower growth in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Construction and property company Lim Kah Ngam said on Wednesday it expected slower growth this year due to a slowdown in the property market.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that barring unforseen circumstances, the directors did not expect the group's results for 1996 to be maintained in 1997.</p>
<p>It reported net profit rose 4.77 percent to Singapore $10.47 million, for the financial year ended December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
